BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315029840@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260725T033826Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260802T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260802T140000
SUMMARY:Alcohol Wars: The Distillery and the Brewery District
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or fo
 r signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticke
 t amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the 
 following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nSummer of 2026
  is upon us\, and a good beer would hit the spot. Well if the water came f
 rom the Don River or Toronto Bay\, what would hit your spot would be Chole
 ra. But let's talk about the good times\, even children drank beer for thi
 s exact reason\, Cholera. So now that you have whet your appetite for some
  good old fashioned drinks and spirits let's dive right in.\n\nIn 1832\, T
 oronto was known as Little York and was to become the City of Toronto in 1
 834\, the Gooderham and Worts Distillery was founded. By the late 1860s an
 d 1870s\, it blossomed into the world's largest distillery.\n\nAnd it's a 
 historic jewel on our waterfront\, a place to stroll\, meetup\, have a cof
 fee or a bite to eat. Come and explore one of Toronto's most fascinating n
 eighbourhoods. And get a bird's eye view of how Toronto developed around t
 he time that Canada became a country in 1867.\n\nBut let's not forget the 
 district to the north. The area near the banks of the Don River on and aro
 und River Street and Queen Street East was the core of the Beer Industry. 
 Let's take a look at how the two industries came together and who was invo
 lved.\n\nFor a quick peek at the walk check out this link on my YouTube ch
 annel at https://youtu.be/xAp97lI_20A\n\nThis walk is for all fitness leve
 ls.\n\nThe meeting place for our walking adventure is opposite the streetc
 ar loop on Cherry Street just south of Mill Street at the eastern edge of 
 the district. Cross Cherry Street and meet at the entrance to Tank House L
 ane.\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person.\n\n\\*\\* **Ple
 ase note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for 
 this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohisto
 rywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315029
 840/
